<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria 3.1 bln levs 15-mth T-notes 40 pct sold.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria 3.1 bln levs 15-mth T-notes 40 pct sold.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's Finance Ministry offer of 3.1 billion levs worth of 15-month floater coupon T-notes was 39.8 percent sold, the central bank (BNB) said.</p>
<p>The paper bears a quarterly coupon equal to the BNB's central interest rate (CIR) for the period to maturity. The CIR is now set at 25 percent monthly or 300 percent annually.</p>
<p>The issue was offered with no minimum acceptable price set in advance by the ministry.</p>
<p>Three financial institutions took part in Friday's auction, the BNB said. The ministry did not say what the cumulative annual yield of the issue was.</p>
<p>Details of the issue follow. Prices are in percent of par:</p>
<p> Issue number		  BG 2032696127</p>
<p> Par value		     3.1 bln levs</p>
<p> Auction date		  September 27, 1996</p>
<p> Issue date		    October 3, 1996</p>
<p> Maturity date		 January 1, 1998</p>
<p> Bids received		 1,235 million levs</p>
<p> Avg price of bids	   54.16 pct</p>
<p> Bids approved		 1,235 million levs</p>
<p> Avg accepted price	  54.16 levs</p>
<p> Interest payments	   January 2, 1997; April 3, 1997;</p>
<p>				   July 3, 1997; October 2, 1997;</p>
<p>				   January 1, 1998</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 981 8569</p>
